  "generated_text": "First, we need to simplify the expression \\(\\frac{x^6 - 16x^3 + 64}{x^3 - 8}\\).\n\nNotice that the numerator can be factored as:\n\\[\nx^6 - 16x^3 + 64 = (x^3 - 8)^2\n\\]\n\nSo, the expression becomes:\n\\[\n\\frac{(x^3 - 8)^2}{x^3 - 8}\n\\]\n\nFor \\(x^3 \\neq 8\\), we can cancel out \\(x^3 - 8\\) from the numerator and the denominator:\n\\[\nx^3 - 8\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to evaluate this expression when \\(x = 6\\):\n\\[\n6^3 - 8\n\\]\n\nCalculate \\(6^3\\):\n\\[\n6^3 = 216\n\\]\n\nThen, from 216:\n\\[\n216 - 8 = 208\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the expression when \\(x = 6\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{208}\n\\]",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[208, '208']",
    "gold_answer": "Note that $\\left(x^3-8\\right)^2=x^6-16x^3+64$. So $\\frac{x^6-16x^3+64}{x^3-8}=\\frac{\\left(x^3-8\\right)^2}{x^3-8}=x^3-8$. So, the answer is $6^3-8=216-8=\\boxed{208}$.",
    "is_correct": true
  },
